@title Lab Result Routing
@subtitle Calder Valley Hospital laboratory informatics: who gets told and when
@date 2026-10-02

!!! Critical values are urgent: phone the ordering clinician within 10 minutes of verification, and get read-back within 15 minutes of the call. Everything else is routine.

# Routing flow
diagram route dir=TB title="How a verified result is routed"
route: start "Result verified in lab system" svc
route: crit "Critical value?" decision focus
route: phone "Phone the ordering clinician" team focus
route: rb "Read back confirmed within 15 minutes?" decision
route: log "Log the read-back" store
route: esc "Escalate to department head" team
route: abn "Flagged abnormal?" decision
route: inbox "Add to clinician inbox" svc
route: file "File without alert" store
route: portal "Release to patient portal" svc
route: start -> crit
route: crit -> phone : yes
route: crit -> abn : no
route: phone -> rb
route: rb -> log : yes
route: rb -> esc : no
route: esc -> log
route: abn -> inbox : yes
route: abn -> file : no
route: inbox -> portal
route: file -> portal
route: group urgent "Urgent: critical values" phone, rb, esc, log
route: group routine "Routine" abn, inbox, file, portal

# Time limits
table = step,limit,priority; Phone call for a critical value,within 10 minutes of verification,**Urgent**; Read-back confirmation,within 15 minutes of the call,**Urgent**; Abnormal result review in clinician inbox,within 1 business day,Routine; Routine result release to patient portal,after 24 hours,Routine; Abnormal result release to patient portal,held 72 hours so the clinician can speak to the patient first,Routine

# Who is called
kpi Weekdays 07:00–19:00 | Ordering clinician
kpi Nights and weekends | Covering physician | via hospital operator
kpi Escalation | Dr. Naomi Eze | department head
